---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, hrefEn as href } from '../../../lib/site';

const enlace = 'text-tinta underline decoration-oro/50 underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-oro-oscuro';
const parrafo = 'mt-4 text-[16px] text-pizarra';
const titulo = 'mt-3 font-display text-[clamp(21px,2.2vw,27px)] font-semibold leading-[1.2]';
const numero = 'font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.14em] text-oro-oscuro';
const lista = 'mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-[16px] text-pizarra marker:text-oro-oscuro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="All the information you provide to us is processed and stored in the European Union, in accordance with the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR)."
>
  <section class="wrap pb-14 pt-20 md:pb-20 md:pt-28">
    <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>Legal</p>
    <h1
      class="mt-5 max-w-[16ch] font-display text-[clamp(38px,6vw,76px)] font-extralight leading-[1.04] tracking-[-0.035em]"
      data-reveal
    >
      Your data in Europe. GDPR compliant.
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-[52ch] text-[clamp(17px,1.6vw,20px)] text-pizarra" data-reveal>
      All the information you provide to us is processed and stored in the European Union, in accordance with the
      GDPR (Regulation (EU) 2016/679) and Spanish Organic Law 3/2018 (LOPDGDD).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="hairline">
    <div class="wrap py-16 md:py-24">
      <article class="max-w-[68ch] space-y-14">
        <section data-reveal>
          <p class={numero}>01</p>
          <h2 class={titulo}>Data controller</h2>
          <p class={parrafo}>
            The controller of your personal data is {site.sociedad}, with tax ID (CIF) {site.cif} and
            registered address at {site.direccion}, a company that trades under the name {site.nombre}.
          </p>
          <p class={parrafo}>
            Contact email for privacy matters: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`} class={enlace}
              >{site.email}</a
            >.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section data-reveal>
          <p class={numero}>02</p>
          <h2 class={titulo}>Data we collect</h2>
          <p class={parrafo}>
            We only collect the data you voluntarily provide to us when you fill in forms,
            book a free assessment or send us an email. This data may include:
          </p>
          <ul class={lista}>
            <li>First name and surname</li>
            <li>Company and job title</li>
            <li>Email address</li>
            <li>Phone number, if you provide it</li>
            <li>Industry and a description of your situation</li>
          </ul>
          <p class={parrafo}>
            When you submit the form we also record the IP address it is sent from, for the sole
            purpose of limiting automated submissions. It is kept together with the message and deleted with it.
          </p>
          <p class={parrafo}>
            To measure website usage we use Umami, a cookieless analytics tool that does not
            identify the visitor or store their IP address: it records, anonymously and in aggregate, page
            views, country, device type and the source of the visit, on our own server in the European
            Union. There are no tracking cookies and no profiling for advertising purposes, and we do not combine this data with external
            sources. You can find the details in the <a href={href('/politica-cookies/')} class={enlace}
              >cookie policy</a
            >.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section data-reveal>
          <p class={numero}>03</p>
          <h2 class={titulo}>Purposes of processing</h2>
          <ul class={lista}>
            <li>To respond to your contact or assessment request.</li>
            <li>To send you tailored commercial proposals if you request them.</li>
            <li>To maintain a contractual relationship if you decide to engage our services.</li>
            <li>To comply with legal and tax obligations.</li>
            <li>To improve our services through aggregated analysis.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section data-reveal>
          <p class={numero}>04</p>
          <h2 class={titulo}>Legal basis for processing</h2>
          <p class={parrafo}>
            The legal basis for processing is your explicit consent, given when you fill in our forms and, where
            applicable, the performance of a contract.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section data-reveal>
          <p class={numero}>05</p>
          <h2 class={titulo}>Data retention</h2>
          <p class={parrafo}>
            We keep your data for as long as necessary to fulfil the stated purposes, unless the law
            requires a different period. For business contacts with no signed contract, the
            data is kept for a maximum of 24 months from the last contact.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section data-reveal>
          <p class={numero}>06</p>
          <h2 class={titulo}>Location and data transfers</h2>
          <p class={parrafo}>
            The pages of this site are static and are served through GitHub Pages, a service of
            GitHub, Inc., which only records technical access data, such as the IP address, in order to provide
            the service. GitHub participates in the EU-US Data Privacy Framework.
          </p>
          <p class={parrafo}>
            The contact form is processed by our own server located in Germany. The
            message is stored there and forwarded from there to our corporate email, hosted on Google Workspace (Google
            Ireland Ltd.). If you write to us directly or book a call, your message and the appointment are
            handled through Google Workspace and Google Calendar under the same conditions.
          </p>
          <p class={parrafo}>
            The systems we build for our clients are hosted on infrastructure in the European
            Union, mainly in Frankfurt, Germany. We do not carry out any other international
            data transfers without the safeguards required by the GDPR.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section data-reveal>
          <p class={numero}>07</p>
          <h2 class={titulo}>Your rights</h2>
          <p class={parrafo}>As a data subject you have the right to:</p>
          <ul class={lista}>
            <li><span class="text-tinta">Access:</span> find out which of your personal data we process.</li>
            <li><span class="text-tinta">Rectification:</span> correct inaccurate or incomplete data.</li>
            <li><span class="text-tinta">Erasure:</span> request the deletion of your data.</li>
            <li><span class="text-tinta">Objection:</span> object to the processing of your data.</li>
            <li><span class="text-tinta">Restriction:</span> request the restriction of processing.</li>
            <li><span class="text-tinta">Portability:</span> receive your data in a structured format.</li>
            <li>
              <span class="text-tinta">Complaint:</span> lodge a complaint with the <a
                href="https://www.aepd.es/"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener"
                class={enlace}>Spanish Data Protection Agency (AEPD)</a
              >.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class={parrafo}>
            To exercise any of these rights, write to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`} class={enlace}
              >{site.email}</a
            > stating who you are and what you are requesting.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section data-reveal>
          <p class={numero}>08</p>
          <h2 class={titulo}>Security</h2>
          <p class={parrafo}>
            We apply reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect your data: encryption in transit
            with HTTPS, restricted access to the corporate email and, in client projects, access
            control and backups on European infrastructure. Even so, no system is completely
            invulnerable, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section data-reveal>
          <p class={numero}>09</p>
          <h2 class={titulo}>Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p class={parrafo}>
            This policy may be updated. The date of the last update appears at the foot of the page. Material
            changes will be notified by email to active contacts.
          </p>
        </section>

        <p class="hairline pt-8 font-mono text-[12px] text-pizarra" data-reveal>
          Last updated: September 2026
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
